SEC. 50101. ONSHORE OIL AND GAS LEASING.

Repeals Inflation Reduction Act provisions that increased onshore oil and gas royalty rates and eliminated noncompetitive leasing, restoring prior law. Requires the Secretary of the Interior to immediately resume quarterly oil and gas lease sales in compliance with the Mineral Leasing Act, with a minimum of 4 sales per fiscal year in each of nine specified states (Wyoming, New Mexico, Colorado, Utah, Montana, North Dakota, Oklahoma, Nevada, Alaska). Mandates that at least 50% of nominated available parcels be offered in each sale, and requires replacement sales if a sale is canceled or if 25% or more of offered acreage receives no bids. Amends the Mineral Leasing Act to require lease sales within 18 months of an expression of interest, limits lease stipulations to those in the approved resource management plan, sets a 4-year non-renewable term for permits to drill, and requires approval of production commingling applications under specified measurement conditions. [end of text]


